    "temple": {
      "note": "山烟寺 inside its 山门: the poplar-ringed yard where the monks train (the pile of bricks on its north side), the gate house with its jade plaque (the great middle door shut, the side doors open), the flagstone road between peonies to the golden 大雄宝殿 and its golden doors; east the small stone path to the herb garden in its plots; in the hall the gilded Buddha on his lotus throne, the censer before him, west the arch to the garden (bridge, rockery, pavilion) and 流云轩 north of it with its tall drawers and the plaques on its walls; behind the yellow curtain the laurel-lined walkway north to the 后殿 (药师如来 and the eighteen arhats painted round) and the two pagodas of the 塔林 east of it; west the walkway along the walls of 流云轩 and the 后殿, painted with 观世音's deeds, to the 香积厨 and its two stoves.",
